    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0293" n="197" xml:id="pg197"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moore to Mr. Denby.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1573.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 2888, of the 17th ultimo, reporting that a mob has killed a native
                    hospital assistant at Chiang Pei and demolished premises rented by American
                    missionaries at that place.</p>
                <p>Your energetic remonstrance to the Tsung-li Yamên and demand for appropriate
                    redress according to the ascertained circumstances are approved by the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
